WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.537
- Just by looking at you, I
can tell what's wrong with you.

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:06.204
(uptempo music)

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.720
You wanna look your best,
and whenever you have

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.360
any imperfection, you're quick

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.720
to blame it on aging or stress.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.460
But really, that's not all the signs

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.850
that something is wrong with your body.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.880
If your insides aren't healthy,

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.790
that will show superficially.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.640
That's why when you come into my office,

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.810
I look at you as a whole.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.230
What warning signs are appearing

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.310
on you superficially that I can figure out

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.500
to lead to a diagnosis?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.070
Before I spill the beans and explain

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.320
to you everything that's going on,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.380
you need to understand how the body works.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.830
It works in a system and it's

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.550
made up of multiple components.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.640
When one of those components doesn't work

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.470
a lot of times that can show signs

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.740
on your physical appearance.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.570
If one part isn't working, another part

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:45.470
of the body compensates that's the way

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.040
your body maintains something,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.966
what we call homeostasis,
a balance of what's normal.

00:00:50.966 --> 00:00:52.460
Wait, wait, wait, one more
thing before we start.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.330
It's important to know
that while I'm giving you

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.200
a lot of physical appearance signs,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.290
it doesn't mean that you have the disease

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.570
if you have one of these.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.940
All it means is that you need to go

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.060
to your doctor and have a conversation.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.560
Something you should be doing anyway

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.860
if you've been watching my videos.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.700
Boom, these are the top physical signs

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.950
that tell me something else
is going on inside your body.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.890
Facial flush or rosy cheeks.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.030
Do you feel like your face
looks a little too red?

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.020
I'm not talking about the
time where you get sunburned

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.020
or when your crush looks at you.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:18.853
Hey girl.

00:01:18.853 --> 00:01:20.770
You may have a medical
condition called Rosacea.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.680
Rosacea's a fairly common skin problem

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.948
with 14 million people living with

00:01:23.948 --> 00:01:26.020
the issue in the United States today.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.870
It's not something you should
get really concerned about

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.520
thinking it's a danger to your health,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.040
but it's a simple benign condition

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.500
that can be treated by your doctor.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.550
Wait, wait, wait one more
thing about facial flush.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.020
If you're part of the Asian population,

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.650
you may suffer from
something called Asian Flush.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.690
That's what happens
when you drink alcohol,

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:41.860
but because you're deficient in

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.304
the enzyme Acetaldehyde Dehydrogenase,

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:47.070
yeah that's a mouthful,
you may have a reaction

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.180
because you can't clear
the alcohol properly.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.630
You may think you have a thin chin,

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.090
you may think you have a thick neck,

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.760
you may think it's just a cosmetic problem

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:54.850
and not that big of a deal.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.490
I think it's a serious risk factor

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.520
for an illness called Sleep Apnea

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.950
which can predispose you
to so many bad illnesses

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.840
including stoke, heart
disease, high blood pressure.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.175
When you have Sleep Apnea,
there's actually moments

00:02:06.175 --> 00:02:08.930
in the night where your
airway completely closes.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:12.460
Whether it's because it's too
small or too big, it closes.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.830
And when that happens it ruins
the quality of your sleep.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.847
We've all heard our
partner's snore at night.

00:02:16.847 --> 00:02:18.800
(loud snoring)
(suspenseful music)

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.030
Or wake up in the middle of the night

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.160
because their breathing wasn't right.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.210
That's Sleep Apnea.

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.980
One of the best lifestyle
changes you can make

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.110
for Sleep Apnea is to lose weight.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:27.540
Unwanted body hair.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.380
Ladies, this is mostly for you.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:32.330
If you start growing hair where
you've never had hair before

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.560
it doesn't mean you should
pay a visit to your spa,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.010
but it does mean you should
pay a visit to your doctor.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:37.843
Why?

00:02:37.843 --> 00:02:39.670
Because that actually has
a medical word behind it,

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.850
it's called hirsutism and what that means

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.561
is you started growing hair in a place

00:02:43.561 --> 00:02:45.550
where men usually grow hair.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.690
This could be due to a hormonal problem.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.960
One of the most common being PCOS

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.310
which is Polycystic Ovarian Syndrome.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.140
When you pair hirsutism
plus abnormal periods,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.540
that's highly suspicious for PCOS.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.200
Hey man, you got stanky breath, bro?

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.860
If you have bad breath,
or what's medically

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:05.340
known as halitosis, it could
be a sign of Acid Reflux.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.660
During Acid Reflux, the stomach contents

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.260
including food, acid, all get pushed up

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.260
into your esophagus and
create this nasty smell

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.190
that you may notice when you
think you have bad breath.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.790
A lot of people think
they'll solve this problem

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.470
by brushing your teeth more,
but that's not the solution.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.370
The solution is to go see your doctor.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.160
Some say the eyes are
the window to the soul.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.300
But what I say, the nails are
the window to your health.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.750
When a patient comes into my office

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.150
and I'm doing a physical exam,

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.580
I pay extra attention to the nails.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.260
The nails give me a lot of information

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.930
on what's going on inside your body

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.490
and tip me off to some illnesses

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.630
I should be on the lookout for.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.110
If you have clubbing of the fingers,

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.810
that could point to a chronic
respiratory infection.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.270
If you have spooning of your nails,

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.450
that could point to a
chronic anemia process.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.000
Some of you may worry
about white marks or lines

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.340
on your nails and generally
that's not a problem.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.580
But if you do have two
lines running parallel

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.770
horizontally across your nail, that could

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.400
be something called Muehrcke's Lines

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.920
and representative of
kidney or liver issues.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.200
Some of you may find dents
or ridges in your nails

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.430
and generally, that's not something

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.740
you should be concerned about.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.840
If that does occur with
some weird symptoms

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.810
at the same time, that's
definitely something

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.300
I wanna hear about and could point

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.980
to a more serious autoimmune issue.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.764
Do you guys remember what
the body's largest organ is?

00:04:16.764 --> 00:04:19.530
- No, no!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.363
- Skin.

00:04:20.363 --> 00:04:21.210
First thing's first, you know how you have

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.910
that little pimple that little scratch

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.180
that never seems to heal?

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.140
To you that may not be of any importance,

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.140
but to me it's incredibly important.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.560
If you have a non-healing
wound of the face

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.140
it's Squamous Cell Carcinoma
until my tests prove otherwise.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:37.273
Also of utmost importance
to skin are moles.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.660
No, no, no, not this type of mole.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.750
- Mole, bloody mole!

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.060
- Yeah, that's the mole I'm talkin' about.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.210
Most of the time moles are
completely harmless and benign.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.000
However, sometimes they may represent

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.640
a serious form of skin cancer.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.010
The way doctors make
this distinction is using

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:56.340
the ABCDE classification
system along with Dermoscopy.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.050
When you're younger it's not
abnormal to form new moles,

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.560
however as you age in
your fifties and sixties,

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.410
if you're still developing new moles

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.000
that could be a cause for concern

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.540
and cause me to investigate further.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.373
Hair.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.980
It's perfectly normal to see
a few strands in the shower,

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:13.470
but if your shower drain
looks like a baby rodent,

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.930
there might be something else going on.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:17.360
Excessive hair loss can
be caused by an overactive

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.200
or underactive thyroid
or something like anemia.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.700
So when a patient walks into my office

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.090
I pay extra attention to
what's going on on their scalp.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.930
However, have no fear,
a lot of these issues

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.300
can be diagnosed by a simple blood test.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.950
Also, it's important to
remember that you're able

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.930
to lose up to a hundred
strands of hair per day

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.244
and that's totally acceptable.

00:05:35.244 --> 00:05:36.950
♪ Look into my eyes ♪

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:39.310
The eyes will give you
a lot of information.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.790
If you look at the color of the eye,

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.290
if there's something off,
it's not perfectly white.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.740
A lot of times you'll see
some yellowing of the eyes

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.080
and it has a medical name
it's called Jaundice.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.380
That occurs when there's something wrong

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.390
with your liver or your gall bladder.

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.990
I could also look below your eye

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.850
and get some extra information.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.860
Things like redness or bags
can represent something

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.840
called Allergic Shiners,
which is a very common

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.180
symptom of people who
suffer with allergies.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.530
Springtime, fall time, very common.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:09.060
If you don't sleep well, if
you eat high sodium foods,

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.530
if you're dehydrated, the
appearance of your eyes

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.690
is gonna appear fatigued, heavy, sad

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.180
and it's not gonna be a pretty sight.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.610
You know what they say
about big feet, right?

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.290
- Yeah, no, yeah, no.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:23.430
- It's important to make sure
that they're not just swollen.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:26.450
That could represent a wide
variety of medical issues.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.180
Things like congestive heart failure,

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.940
circulation issues, lung issues,

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:33.030
autoimmune things like arthritis.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.670
All of those can lead
your legs to balloon up.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:38.610
But, if you have some mild
swelling at the end of a long day

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.650
of being on your feet,
that's something called

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.890
Dependent Edema and likely
nothing to worry about.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.510
A lot of these signs I've pointed out

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.660
may seem like superficial concerns,

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.720
but they truly tell me a whole story

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.740
of what's going on inside your body.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.380
Never be afraid to tell your doctor

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.160
if something doesn't
feel right, look right

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:56.170
or even smell right.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.598
If you have any questions
in the meanwhile,

00:06:57.598 --> 00:07:00.270
drop me a comment down below,
we'll have a conversation

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.730
and figure out what's going on.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.800
Otherwise, make sure to
hit subscribe and share

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.336
this channel with your friends and family.

00:07:06.336 --> 00:07:07.169
(static)

00:07:07.169 --> 00:07:08.574
(loud breathing)

00:07:08.574 --> 00:07:09.407
(static)

00:07:09.407 --> 00:07:11.080
Those people over there
are a little weird.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:11.914
Oh wait, that's me.

00:07:11.914 --> 00:07:12.747
(static)

00:07:12.747 --> 00:07:13.930
The food that's supposed
to be in your belly

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.440
along with the acid gets regurgitated back

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:17.870
into your esophagus which creates

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.383
that nasty smell you hear.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:21.837
(people laughing)

